WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.541 --> 00:00:32.416
<b>In the previous verse, we learned</b>

2
00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:36.458
<b>that this spiritual knowledge of</b>
<b>the Gita is the most ancient,</b>

3
00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:41.500
<b>and Lord Krishna himself imparted this </b>
<b>wisdom to Surya, the Sun God,</b>

4
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.041
<b>which then reached humanity through Manu.</b>

5
00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:45.750
<b>However,</b>

6
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.375
<b>this naturally raises a question -</b>

7
00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:53.333
<b>if this knowledge is so ancient </b>
<b>and has existed for ages,</b>

8
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:57.708
<b>why did it need to be revived?</b>

9
00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:00.666
<b>This verse answers precisely that question.</b>

10
00:01:05.541 --> 00:01:08.125
<b>In this verse, Krishna says,</b>

11
00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:11.041
<b>"Arjuna, this spiritual knowledge of yoga,</b>

12
00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:17.125
<b>was passed down from generation to generation</b>
<b> to sage-like kings as a sacred tradition.</b>

13
00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:21.041
<b>However, with the passage of time, </b>
<b>this wisdom vanished from the world."</b>

14
00:01:21.041 --> 00:01:24.625
<b>This speaks of the guru-disciple tradition,</b>

15
00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:29.500
<b>where a teacher passed this knowledge to</b>
<b>their student of the next generation.</b>

16
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.666
<b>When generations changed, </b>
<b>that student became a teacher,</b>

17
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:35.791
<b>continuing this tradition forward.</b>

18
00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:38.250
<b>Think of it like a chain of iron links –</b>

19
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:47.750
<b>each connection between guru and disciple</b>
<b>served as a link, carrying this knowledge forward.</b>

20
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.125
<b>For instance,</b>

21
00:01:49.125 --> 00:01:54.583
<b>Sir Isaac Newton discovered </b>
<b>gravity centuries ago,</b>

22
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:58.291
<b>others learned from him, wrote books about it,</b>

23
00:01:58.291 --> 00:02:01.083
<b>our teachers understood it in school,</b>

24
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:04.125
<b>and eventually, this knowledge reached us.</b>

25
00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:06.958
<b>The same happened with spiritual knowledge.</b>

26
00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:14.416
<b>But what happens if a link in </b>
<b>this chain breaks or weakens?</b>

27
00:02:14.416 --> 00:02:18.916
<b>What if a disciple fails to</b>
<b>fully grasp a spiritual truth,</b>

28
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>and then, when they become a teacher,</b>

29
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:25.250
<b>transmits that incomplete </b>
<b>knowledge to their student?</b>

30
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.916
<b>We're talking about thousands of years here,</b>

31
00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:30.916
<b>with countless links of </b>
<b>guru-disciple relationships.</b>

32
00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.125
<b>Naturally,</b>

33
00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:35.958
<b>any knowledge can become clouded over time.</b>

34
00:02:35.958 --> 00:02:41.375
<b>And when things reach a point where </b>
<b>knowledge stands at the brink of extinction,</b>

35
00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:47.708
<b>who better to revive it than the </b>
<b>supreme source of that knowledge itself?</b>

36
00:02:47.708 --> 00:02:54.500
<b>Just as Krishna is now personally coming forward</b>
<b>to revive this wisdom of the Gita.</b>

37
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.833
<b>This dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna </b>
<b>wasn't limited to the context of war;</b>

38
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:04.166
<b>it was meant to influence all of future humanity.</b>

39
00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:07.625
<b>Consider how, even centuries </b>
<b>after the Mahabharata,</b>

40
00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:12.416
<b>this wisdom continues to </b>
<b>guide us through life's challenges.</b>

41
00:03:12.416 --> 00:03:20.000
<b>Here, Krishna also mentions the ancient Rajarshis</b>
<b>- kings who were like sages.</b>

42
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.000
<b>Can a king be a sage?</b>

43
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.458
<b>Absolutely,</b>

44
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:26.625
<b>in fact, that's how it should be.</b>

45
00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:27.916
<b>Think about it –</b>

46
00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:33.500
<b>what is the true purpose of a king </b>
<b>or anyone in a leadership position?</b>

47
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:39.375
<b>Isn't it to make life easier for their subjects?</b>

48
00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:43.000
<b>If this is the true purpose, </b>
<b>it requires not selfishness</b>

49
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.000
<b>but values focused on social welfare,</b>

50
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:52.708
<b>which is only possible when the ruler</b>
<b>is selfless and spiritually enlightened.</b>

51
00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:56.833
<b>This is why this knowledge was </b>
<b>entrusted to sage-like kings.</b>

52
00:03:56.833 --> 00:04:00.500
<b>Here, Krishna also illustrates </b>
<b>the adverse effects of time.</b>

53
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.083
<b>Think of it like milk left in the open –</b>

54
00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:10.166
<b>after some time, it spoils due </b>
<b>to environmental effects.</b>

55
00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:17.583
<b>To preserve that milk, we need to make efforts, </b>
<b>provide the right cool environment.</b>

56
00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:18.708
<b>Similarly,</b>

57
00:04:18.708 --> 00:04:20.500
<b>without proper effort,</b>

58
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:25.708
<b>knowledge too can become </b>
<b>corrupted under negative influences.</b>

59
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:27.000
<b>This corruption did occur,</b>

60
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.791
<b>leading to the war of Mahabharata.</b>

61
00:04:31.791 --> 00:04:34.208
<b>Krishna himself had to come forward</b>

62
00:04:34.208 --> 00:04:38.500
<b>to start a new chain of this knowledge.</b>

63
00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.583
<b>Environment</b>

64
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:49.041
<b>and time –</b>

65
00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:53.083
<b>never underestimate their forces.</b>

66
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:58.083
<b>If regular care is not given,</b>

67
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:01.666
<b>things are bound to break down.</b>

68
00:05:01.666 --> 00:05:11.416
<b>this spiritual wisdom too had become clouded </b>
<b>by the influence of time and surroundings.</b>

69
00:05:11.416 --> 00:05:14.083
<b>I had to return</b>

70
00:05:14.083 --> 00:05:17.958
<b>to revive this knowledge.</b>

71
00:05:17.958 --> 00:05:23.125
<b>Isn't this exactly what happens</b>
<b> in your personal life?</b>

72
00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:24.875
<b>Think about it.</b>

73
00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:29.791
<b>You make a resolution, set a goal,</b>

74
00:05:29.791 --> 00:05:34.541
<b>but with time, that resolve breaks</b>

75
00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:38.291
<b>and the objective remains unfulfilled.</b>

76
00:05:38.291 --> 00:05:40.791
<b>Happens quite often, doesn't it?</b>

77
00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:42.583
<b>For instance,</b>

78
00:05:42.583 --> 00:05:45.833
<b>you decided to improve your health,</b>

79
00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:51.291
<b>set a goal to become healthier this year.</b>

80
00:05:51.291 --> 00:05:53.791
<b>You made some decisions –</b>

81
00:05:53.791 --> 00:05:55.333
<b>regular exercise,</b>

82
00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:58.500
<b>staying away from sweets, and so on.</b>

83
00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.458
<b>Everything went well for the first few days</b>

84
00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:04.541
<b>but then... laziness crept in,</b>

85
00:06:04.541 --> 00:06:06.666
<b>you skipped exercise, or</b>

86
00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:09.666
<b>perhaps a tempting dessert appeared,</b>

87
00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:13.166
<b>and you couldn't resist. And there,</b>

88
00:06:13.166 --> 00:06:15.125
<b>the chain broke.</b>

89
00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:19.875
<b>The goal remained incomplete.</b>

90
00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:22.291
<b>Now what?</b>

91
00:06:22.291 --> 00:06:25.625
<b>Should you blame yourself?</b>

92
00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:27.041
<b>No.</b>

93
00:06:27.041 --> 00:06:29.416
<b>Remember this –</b>

94
00:06:29.416 --> 00:06:34.375
<b>time and environment will </b>
<b>always have their influence.</b>

95
00:06:34.375 --> 00:06:39.416
<b>The chain of resolution will break sometimes,</b>

96
00:06:39.416 --> 00:06:40.625
<b>but</b>

97
00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:43.291
<b>you must rise again.</b>

98
00:06:43.291 --> 00:06:46.125
<b>Recall your purpose,</b>

99
00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:55.708
<b>revive your determination, </b>
<b>and begin a new chain.</b>

100
00:06:55.708 --> 00:06:57.083
<b>Think about it...</b>

101
00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.333
<b>what's better?</b>

102
00:06:59.333 --> 00:07:02.416
<b>Lamenting over a broken chain,</b>

103
00:07:02.416 --> 00:07:04.416
<b>cursing yourself,</b>

104
00:07:04.416 --> 00:07:07.250
<b>leaving it broken</b>

105
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.125
<b>Or is it better</b>

106
00:07:09.125 --> 00:07:12.250
<b>to mend that chain</b>

107
00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:19.166
<b>and put your resolutions back into action?</b>

108
00:07:19.166 --> 00:07:23.541
<b>I have reconnected this chain of the Gita;</b>

109
00:07:23.541 --> 00:07:24.541
<b>you</b>

110
00:07:24.541 --> 00:07:27.250
<b>should reconnect the chain of your resolutions.</b>

111
00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:31.916
<b>Rise, begin today itself.</b>

112
00:07:36.541 --> 00:07:40.958
<b>The influence of time and environment,</b>

113
00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:43.791
<b>the loss of knowledge,</b>

114
00:07:43.791 --> 00:07:47.750
<b>and my reappearance once again</b>

115
00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:55.708
<b>were necessary to re-establish </b>
<b>the spiritual wisdom of the Gita.</b>

116
00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:56.750
<b>And</b>

117
00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:02.500
<b>such circumstances can arise not only </b>
<b>in the context of spiritual knowledge</b>

118
00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:08.458
<b>but also in family or social life.</b>

119
00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:10.125
<b>Imagine,</b>

120
00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:12.875
<b>if not given proper attention,</b>

121
00:08:12.875 --> 00:08:16.208
<b>like other aspects of life,</b>

122
00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:24.458
<b>how family or social relationships </b>
<b>can weaken over time.</b>

123
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:27.625
<b>Time passes,</b>

124
00:08:27.625 --> 00:08:33.666
<b>you become busy with your life or business,</b>

125
00:08:33.666 --> 00:08:36.166
<b>and then, after a long while,</b>

126
00:08:36.166 --> 00:08:38.333
<b>you realize</b>

127
00:08:38.333 --> 00:08:47.208
<b>that the deep connection you once had with </b>
<b>your life partner or a friend has</b>

128
00:08:47.208 --> 00:08:51.000
<b>now weakened.</b>

129
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:56.916
<b>Just as the Gita emphasizes the need</b>
<b>to revive spiritual teachings,</b>

130
00:08:56.916 --> 00:08:58.041
<b>similarly,</b>

131
00:08:58.041 --> 00:09:07.875
<b>we must also strive to keep our relationships </b>
<b>with loved ones fresh and vibrant.</b>

132
00:09:07.875 --> 00:09:10.875
<b>The crucial aspects here</b>

133
00:09:10.875 --> 00:09:17.375
<b>are regular self-reflection and continuous effort.</b>

134
00:09:17.375 --> 00:09:20.583
<b>It is not enough to merely form relationships;</b>

135
00:09:20.583 --> 00:09:24.333
<b>they must be nurtured,</b>

136
00:09:24.333 --> 00:09:29.166
<b>which requires regular care.</b>

137
00:09:29.166 --> 00:09:30.416
<b>For this,</b>

138
00:09:30.416 --> 00:09:34.500
<b>you must periodically reflect</b>

139
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.625
<b>on whether any relationship is weakening</b>
<b>or on the verge of breaking.</b>

140
00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:41.291
<b>If so,</b>

141
00:09:41.291 --> 00:09:44.625
<b>you must try again,</b>

142
00:09:44.625 --> 00:09:51.041
<b>giving the withering plant of </b>
<b>that relationship the water of time</b>

143
00:09:51.041 --> 00:09:54.708
<b>and the sunlight of love.</b>

144
00:09:54.708 --> 00:09:57.000
<b>For example,</b>

145
00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.291
<b>if self-reflection reveals</b>

146
00:10:00.291 --> 00:10:04.708
<b>that you have grown distant</b>
<b>from an elderly relative,</b>

147
00:10:04.708 --> 00:10:12.958
<b>make an effort to reconnect with them, </b>
<b>maintain regular contact,</b>

148
00:10:12.958 --> 00:10:18.208
<b>or celebrate family festivals together and so on.</b>

149
00:10:18.208 --> 00:10:23.416
<b>These actions will help strengthen the bond.</b>

150
00:10:23.416 --> 00:10:27.375
<b>Such efforts ensure</b>

151
00:10:27.375 --> 00:10:34.583
<b>that family relationships do not weaken </b>
<b>despite the busyness of modern life.</b>

152
00:10:34.583 --> 00:10:35.666
<b>And</b>

153
00:10:35.666 --> 00:10:37.416
<b>remember,</b>

154
00:10:37.416 --> 00:10:42.791
<b>don't do this out of a sense </b>
<b>of burden or duty alone.</b>

155
00:10:42.791 --> 00:10:44.083
<b>Business,</b>

156
00:10:44.083 --> 00:10:49.166
<b>life's rat race, victories, </b>
<b>and defeats are all transient,</b>

157
00:10:49.166 --> 00:10:52.250
<b>dependent on many circumstances.</b>

158
00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.375
<b>But</b>

159
00:10:53.375 --> 00:11:00.416
<b>mutual love and relationships </b>
<b>depend only on two people.</b>

160
00:11:00.416 --> 00:11:08.333
<b>Do your part to maintain the </b>
<b>sweetness of relationships.</b>

161
00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:13.000
<b>Humans are social and familial beings,</b>

162
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:22.625
<b>and those who have sweet relationships</b>
<b>with others will naturally lead a joyful life.</b>

163
00:11:22.625 --> 00:11:28.875
<b>Everyone goes through good and bad times.</b>

164
00:11:28.875 --> 00:11:36.125
<b>During tough times, it is these relationships </b>
<b>that become your support and strength.</b>

165
00:11:36.125 --> 00:11:39.833
<b>Don't neglect them.</b>

166
00:11:39.833 --> 00:11:43.291
<b>Pay attention to this chain of relationships,</b>

167
00:11:43.291 --> 00:11:46.958
<b>and if it is weakening,</b>

168
00:11:46.958 --> 00:11:52.958
<b>it is better to mend it before it breaks.</b>

169
00:11:52.958 --> 00:11:55.500
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

170
00:12:00.375 --> 00:12:03.708
<b>Under the guru-disciple tradition,</b>

171
00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:06.000
<b>this spiritual knowledge of the Gita</b>

172
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:10.250
<b>was passed down from one </b>
<b>generation to the next,</b>

173
00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.625
<b>the tree expanded,</b>

174
00:12:12.625 --> 00:12:18.041
<b>and then gradually, this knowledge </b>
<b>also became obscured.</b>

175
00:12:18.041 --> 00:12:20.000
<b>That's what happens, right?</b>

176
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:25.958
<b>As a tree grows, there's a thick trunk, </b>
<b>then some large branches,</b>

177
00:12:25.958 --> 00:12:28.708
<b>smaller branches within them,</b>

178
00:12:28.708 --> 00:12:32.333
<b>and finally, weak leaves...</b>

179
00:12:32.333 --> 00:12:35.250
<b>As the tree spreads,</b>

180
00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.125
<b>each new branch that grows</b>

181
00:12:38.125 --> 00:12:43.375
<b>becomes farther from the </b>
<b>previous branches, weaker.</b>

182
00:12:43.375 --> 00:12:45.625
<b>If watered regularly,</b>

183
00:12:45.625 --> 00:12:47.541
<b>everything will remain connected,</b>

184
00:12:47.541 --> 00:12:48.625
<b>but</b>

185
00:12:48.625 --> 00:12:51.625
<b>if this tree is not nourished,</b>

186
00:12:51.625 --> 00:12:55.041
<b>the leaves will fall first,</b>

187
00:12:55.041 --> 00:12:57.041
<b>then the small branches,</b>

188
00:12:57.041 --> 00:13:04.708
<b>and eventually, only the tree's dry </b>
<b>trunk will remain alone.</b>

189
00:13:04.708 --> 00:13:09.000
<b>Consider an organization in this context.</b>

190
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.500
<b>When an organization is new,</b>

191
00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:17.875
<b>its founders have a fresh enthusiasm </b>
<b>and ideal business values.</b>

192
00:13:17.875 --> 00:13:27.500
<b>They know how crucial it is to remain focused on </b>
<b>the goal, to have mutual respect and cooperation. </b>

193
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:31.875
<b>This group of founders is like the trunk of a tree.</b>

194
00:13:31.875 --> 00:13:33.333
<b>But then,</b>

195
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:36.541
<b>gradually, as this tree grows,</b>

196
00:13:36.541 --> 00:13:41.750
<b>as the organization expands, new branches join.</b>

197
00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:46.916
<b>And each new branch moves farther </b>
<b>away from the tree's trunk,</b>

198
00:13:46.916 --> 00:13:54.916
<b>unable to keep alive those business values that </b>
<b>once formed the organization's foundation.</b>

199
00:13:54.916 --> 00:14:01.625
<b>Often, new colleagues join the organization </b>
<b>not for a greater purpose,</b>

200
00:14:01.625 --> 00:14:02.458
<b>but</b>

201
00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:07.166
<b>solely for their personal growth.</b>

202
00:14:07.166 --> 00:14:08.583
<b>And then,</b>

203
00:14:08.583 --> 00:14:11.291
<b>like a leaf,</b>

204
00:14:11.291 --> 00:14:14.125
<b>they break away from the organization.</b>

205
00:14:14.125 --> 00:14:15.666
<b>What should be done?</b>

206
00:14:15.666 --> 00:14:20.666
<b>Just as a tree is kept healthy by watering it,</b>

207
00:14:20.666 --> 00:14:26.791
<b>it is necessary for the founders and </b>
<b>senior officials of that organization</b>

208
00:14:26.791 --> 00:14:33.750
<b>to regularly attempt to water the</b>
<b>roots of the organization themselves.</b>

209
00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.958
<b>There are several ways to do this.</b>

210
00:14:36.958 --> 00:14:43.250
<b>They must become living examples </b>
<b>of the organization's values,</b>

211
00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:48.833
<b>adhere to truth and respect in their every action,</b>

212
00:14:48.833 --> 00:14:53.416
<b>and encourage people in every interaction.</b>

213
00:14:53.416 --> 00:14:57.375
<b>They must propagate the organization's values.</b>

214
00:14:57.375 --> 00:14:59.041
<b>At the same time,</b>

215
00:14:59.041 --> 00:15:05.500
<b>the new collaborators and the new leaves, from </b>
<b>which the tree's trunk has been growing distant,</b>

216
00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:11.166
<b>must be regularly connected with.</b>

217
00:15:11.166 --> 00:15:14.250
<b>This will not only keep the organization strong</b>

218
00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.083
<b>but also</b>

219
00:15:15.083 --> 00:15:24.333
<b>provide founders and senior officials with a fresh perspective by constantly meeting new people.</b>

220
00:15:24.333 --> 00:15:31.333
<b>All of this is necessary to keep an </b>
<b>organization's sprawling tree robust.</b>

221
00:15:31.333 --> 00:15:33.166
<b>Reflect on this</b>

222
00:15:33.166 --> 00:15:36.333
<b>and put it into practice.</b>

